Keep merely shareable buffer objects in the bo cache.

FD_BO_SHARED is created as a hint that a bo may be exported later
(freedreno_drmif.h says exactly that), but the msm cache and fence paths treated
it as proof that the bo already had consumers outside the userspace fence
tracking. In this port AIR sets PIPE_BIND_SHARED on every page-sized-or-larger
MTLBuffer because any such buffer can later have a linear texture laid over it;
the result was that nearly every ordinary Metal buffer was born uncacheable and
took a complete kernel gemNew/gemClose cycle.

Split the two states. FD_BO_SHARED remains the allocation-time shareability
hint: it still prevents heap suballocation, because a suballocated bo has no
handle of its own to export. The new internal _FD_BO_EXPORTED bit is set only
when the bo is imported or when fd_bo_get_name(), fd_bo_handle() or
fd_bo_dmabuf() actually exports it. Cache admission, userspace-fence state,
implicit-sync decisions and the read-only prefault exception key off the
actual-exported bit. An unexported shareable bo therefore keeps complete
userspace fence tracking and can be reused through the normal cache; once any
handle is exported the old conservative path applies immediately, including
NO_CACHE and bo_flush() in the export helpers.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_drmif.h b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_drmif.h
--- a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_drmif.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_drmif.h
@@ -123,12 +123,18 @@
